{"name":"Toasted Grain","hex":"#c5a986","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"toasted","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Cooked by toasting.","Very hot."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of toast"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/toasted"},{"term":"grain","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The harvested seeds of various grass food crops, especially wheat, maize, rye, barley, and rice.","Similar seeds from any food crop, e.g., buckwheat, amaranth, quinoa."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To feed grain to.","To make granular; to form into grains."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grain"}],"entries":[{"title":"Toast (food)","blocks":[{"text":"Toast is sliced bread that has been browned by radiant heat. The browning is the result of a Maillard reaction altering the flavor of the bread and making it crispier in texture. The firm surface is easier to spread toppings on and the warmth can help spreads such as butter reach their melting point. Toasting is a common method of making stale bread more palatable. Bread is commonly toasted using devices specifically designed for such, e.g., a toaster or a toaster oven. Toast may contain more acrylamide, caused by the browning process, which is suspected to be a carcinogen. However, claims that acrylamide in burnt food causes cancer have not been proven."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Toast-3.jpg/330px-Toast-3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toast_(food)"},{"title":"Grain","blocks":[{"text":"A grain is a small, hard, dry fruit (caryopsis)–with or without an attached hull layer–harvested for human or animal consumption. A grain crop is a grain-producing plant. The two main types of commercial grain crops are cereals and legumes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Dhaniyangal.jpg/330px-Dhaniyangal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grain"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Toaster.jpg/500px-Toaster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Toaster.jpg/1280px-Toaster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Toaster.jpg/500px-Toaster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A classic two-slot toaster","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AToaster.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Vegemite_and_jelly.jpg/500px-Vegemite_and_jelly.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Vegemite_and_jelly.jpg/1280px-Vegemite_and_jelly.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Vegemite_and_jelly.jpg/500px-Vegemite_and_jelly.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Left: Toast with butter and Vegemite. Right: With butter and strawberry jam.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVegemite_and_jelly.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Toasts_photographed_in_West_Bengal%2C_India.jpg/500px-Toasts_photographed_in_West_Bengal%2C_India.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Toasts_photographed_in_West_Bengal%2C_India.jpg/1280px-Toasts_photographed_in_West_Bengal%2C_India.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/th